# WHAT THIS FILE IS: a template (example) of the .env file. .env holds secret API keys as NAME=value lines.
# app.py calls load_dotenv() (python-dotenv), which copies these lines into the environment, and then
# os.getenv("GOOGLE_API_KEY") / os.getenv("GROQ_API_KEY") read them.
# Analogy: this file is the empty form; your .env is the filled-in form you keep private.
# .env is listed in .gitignore, so git never uploads it. This .example file has only fake values, so it is safe to share.
# Keys typed into the app's sidebar are used first; these .env values are only the fallback.
# Overall flow: copy .env.example -> rename to .env -> paste real keys -> load_dotenv() -> os.getenv() in app.py
# Copy this file, rename it to ".env", and fill in your real API keys.
# NEVER commit the real .env file to GitHub — it contains your secret keys!

# Embeddings (Google AI Studio): https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# GOOGLE_API_KEY = key for Google's embedding model (models/gemini-embedding-001). Real Google keys start
# with "AIza". Used in rag_engine.py to turn chunks and questions into embeddings.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza-your-google-api-key-here

# Answer generation (Groq): https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY = key for Groq, which runs the answer model openai/gpt-oss-20b. Real Groq keys start with "gsk_".
# Used for every answer and for the 3-bullet summary.
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your-groq-api-key-here
